# The sample uploads are fixtures the acceptance gate checks byte for byte.
#
# Scoped to samples/ deliberately. An open action item intends a repo-wide CRLF
# renormalisation, and that pass would rewrite line endings inside these files —
# which changes the signature bytes of the .xls, the deflate stream of the .png,
# and the byte-exact comparison scripts/build-samples.mjs makes. A corrupted
# fixture would fail as "the application rejects its own sample", which reads as
# a broken application rather than a broken checkout.
#
# The repo-wide renormalisation stays that action item's work; this only stops it
# taking the samples with it.
samples/*.pdf binary
samples/*.png binary
samples/*.jpg binary
samples/*.xls binary
samples/*.xlsx binary

# The CSV samples are text, and their CRLF line endings are deliberate: RFC 4180
# specifies them, and build-samples.mjs writes them. Marked -text so no
# normalisation rewrites them into LF and breaks the byte comparison.
samples/*.csv -text

# The wordmark, for the same reason and against the same future pass. Git
# already infers binary from the NUL bytes, so this changes nothing today —
# it is here so a repo-wide `* text=auto` cannot decide otherwise later.
public/*.png binary
